// ISA2 -- a three-thread cumulativity chain with dependencies throughout.
//
// rmm-zoo property: mca (Atomicity / Multicopy atomic).
// Source: Sarkar et al., "Understanding POWER Multiprocessors" (PLDI 2011);
//         Alglave et al., "Herding Cats" (TOPLAS 2014).
//
// P0 writes x then y. P1 reads y and (data dep) writes z. P2 reads z and
// (address dep) reads x. Seeing y=1 and z=1 but x=0 requires the chain
// W(x,1) -> W(y,1) -> R(y) -> W(z) -> R(z) -> R(x) to be broken at the point
// where P0's write to x must have propagated: a non-multicopy-atomic behaviour
// once every intra-thread edge in the chain is a preserved dependency.
//
// Note the leading po edge W(x,1) -> W(y,1) in P0 is NOT a dependency, so
// POWER/ARM need an lwsync there; this file records the dependency-only version,
// which those architectures allow for that reason alone. ISA2+Fsc+Fsc in
// litmus-tests/test6/ is the fenced counterpart.
//
// Reference verdicts: POWER, ARMv7, ARMv8 ALLOW (unfenced P0). SC FORBIDS.
x := 0;
y := 0;
z := 0;
{
  x := 1;
  y := 1
} ||| {
  r1 := y;
  z := r1
} ||| {
  r2 := z;
  rq := &x;
  r3 := *(rq + (r2 - r2))
}
%%
allow (r1 = 1 && r2 = 1 && r3 = 0) [Power]
